      "created_at": "2012-04-04T14:57:39.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Okay, just so I’m perfectly clear on this, when playing The Chairman;</p>\n<ol>\n<li>At the end of the villain turn, Operative brings out an underboss. The turn is over, the underboss’s end of turn effect does not activate.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>or</p>\n<ol start=\"2\">\n<li>Operative brings out an underboss, it is still the end of the villain turn, so the underboss’s end of turn effect is activated, bringing out a thug, which also has an end of turn effect, and that effect is activated too.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>This has been driving me and my friends insane.</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:35:15.886Z",
